From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WIndFate <windfate@vip.qq.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a pipeline cache whose stored shader fails to compile

MVKPipelineCache::readData() compiles every stored shader library while
vkCreatePipelineCache() runs. The Metal compiler reports a failure on
the owner of the library, which is the pipeline cache, so one entry
that fails to compile makes vkCreatePipelineCache() destroy the cache
and return VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED with VK_NULL_HANDLE.

Such an entry is written whenever a pipeline's shader failed to compile
in the run that saved the cache: the shader library is cached even
though its compile failed. Feeding that data back, as an application
does on its next start, then fails cache creation. Drivers on other
platforms do not fail here, and an application that then passes the
null handle to vkGetPipelineCacheData() crashes in
MVKPipelineCache::writeData().

Clear the configuration result after each stored entry is added. The
compile failure is still logged, and a pipeline that uses the entry
still fails as it did when the entry was saved. A read error after the
entry still fails cache creation as before.

This is a Runeon downstream fix, written for this patch series and not
taken from a fork. It has no environment switch: it acts only where the
base fails vkCreatePipelineCache(), and building without the patch
restores the base behaviour.
---
 MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKPipeline.mm | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKPipeline.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKPipeline.mm
index fd85c6d8..e64d6555 100644
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKPipeline.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKPipeline.mm
@@ -2752,6 +2752,13 @@ static void setDepthClipConfig(SPIRVToMSLConversionConfiguration& shaderConfig,
 					addPerformanceInterval(getPerformanceStats().pipelineCache.readPipelineCache, startTime);
 					slCache->addShaderLibrary(&shaderConversionConfig, resultInfo, compressedMSL);
 
+					// Downstream change: Metal can fail to compile a stored entry, as it failed when the
+					// entry was added. That failure is already logged, and a pipeline that uses the entry
+					// still fails as it did then. It must not fail vkCreatePipelineCache, which returns no
+					// cache, for data that vkGetPipelineCacheData returned. A later read error still fails.
+					// ponytail: the failed entry stays in the cache and is compiled again on every load.
+					clearConfigurationResult();
+
 					break;
 				}
 
